      "note": "NOT the deployment cost of this recognizer, and NOT comparable with the stt_whisper figure in a V4 folder. The probe is a synthetic tone. Whisper had no words to find in it, decoded against its own prompt and ran until its 30 s window filled, so a V4 number here measured a failure mode; Parakeet's TDT decoder emits blanks over the same tone and stops, so a V5 number here measures close to the encoder floor. Both are valid device-to-device comparisons for one engine and neither is an engine-to-engine comparison. The live pipeline never submits unvoiced audio: Silero gates it first. For the recognizer cost on real speech, and for the only defensible Whisper-versus-Parakeet timing, use audio_latency_summary.json from Full_Pipeline_Audio_Benchmark.py, which drives 44 committed WAV clips. This stage is kept because the assembled-utterance estimate below is built from it."
